Hi Roger,

Many thanks for the comments; they are very helpful. Can you send me the 
solution to the exercise then?

Also, I often compare models to determine whehter a predictor has a sig. 
effect. Can I determine a main effect by model comparison when random 
slopes are included? For instance, with the following models:

fit.0 = lmer (y ~ 1 + (1|subject)+(1|item))
fit.x = lmer (y ~ x + (1|subject)+(1|item))
fit.xs = lmer (y ~ x + (x-1|subject)+(1|item))

If I want to determine whether x has a sig. effect, which the following 
do I do?

anova (fit.0, fit.x)

or

anova (fit.0, fit.xs)

thanks,

garry


